i-Blackburn vote further rather than help Green.", "watch": "A consolidated independent exit or a major Blackburn misstep could narrow the margin, though a Green win would require a shift far beyond anything polls or markets currently show.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Bill Lee (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Tennessee's governorship is open this year as term-limited Bill Lee steps aside, and Republican Marsha Blackburn is the strong favorite against Democrat Jerri Green in a state that leans Republican by double digits. Recent polls from September and August show Blackburn ahead by nine to thirteen points, consistent with surveys dating back to 2025.\n\nAll six expert ratings call the race Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Blackburn roughly a 93-95 percent chance. A crowded field of independent candidates, including Lauren Pinkston, has drawn headlines and even a request from Green that one independent withdraw, but there is no evidence this changes the underlying dynamics. The forecast expects Blackburn to win comfortably, with Green needing a dramatic, unforeseen shift to make this competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -11.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0463, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0186, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0193, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0336, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0245, "margin": -12.0}]}